# Auto commit + push (Elegance)

When Maro requests any code change for the Elegance Dental Lab project, after finishing the work:

1. Stage only the files related to that change.
2. Create a concise commit (follow repo commit style; do not ask first).
3. Push to `fork` immediately (`git push -u fork HEAD` or current tracking remote that works).
4. If `origin` push fails (403), note that a PR/merge to `ussskils22-prog/main` is still needed — do not block on origin.
5. Never force-push; never amend unless the existing amend rules are fully met.
6. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, tokens).
7. Briefly tell Maro the commit hash and push result when done.

This overrides the default "only commit when asked" preference for this project only when a coding change was actually made.
